Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Watching Two Qubits at Once: Measurement-Induced Entanglement in the \
Quantum-Bayesian Picture\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Two qubits that never interact can be entangled by a measurement \
alone, if the measurement is built so it cannot tell ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"01"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 StyleBox[" from ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"10"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 StyleBox[". A single probe that reflects off both qubits reads out only the \
parity group, sorting the four computational states into three bins, ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 StyleBox[", ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 StyleBox[", and the odd pair, and each noisy record steers the pair \
stochastically into one of the three. This essay builds the two-qubit \
quantum-Bayesian update from the single-qubit one and runs it: we watch the \
odd-parity coherence ride along on the geometric mean of its two populations, \
exactly the single-qubit purity ride-along one level up, watch one record \
climb into a Bell state while its siblings collapse to a product state, and \
pull the concurrence distribution out of an ensemble of records. It is \
bimodal, a spike at zero and a peak that presses against a sharp ceiling, and \
that ceiling is the closed-form maximum concurrence, the entanglement of the \
most fortunate record, which we recover from the simulated envelope. A final \
step traces the same update to the remote-qubit experiments it models and to \
the entanglement essay's place beside the non-commuting one.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: August 18, 2026)", "Text",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Essay Flows", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["\<\
This essay is a computation-first tour of two qubits entangled by a joint \
continuous measurement and nothing else: how the two-qubit Bayesian update is \
the single-qubit one repeated on a larger state, why a measurement that hides \
the odd-parity subspace projects into a Bell state, how a single noisy record \
steers the pair, why the concurrence it can reach is capped in closed form, \
and what sets that cap. Every claim is computed on the spot from base Wolfram \
Language, so nothing here rests on a formula you cannot immediately test and \
change.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell["\<\
In other words, I have tried to build a small laboratory for entanglement by \
measurement. I strongly believe in a computation-first narrative for \
learning: in a sense, if I cannot compute it, I cannot claim to understand \
it. The rhythm throughout is concept, then computation, then interpretation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["\<\
The environment you see is a live Wolfram notebook. Evaluate the cells from \
top to bottom; the toolkit defined in the next section is used by every \
section that follows, so those dependencies matter. A couple of cells run \
small Monte-Carlo ensembles and take a few seconds. My suggestion is to focus \
on the output and its meaning first, then unpack the input code. You are not \
locked into any of it: change the rates, the step, the seed, and rerun your \
own experiments.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the two-qubit door into the continuous-measurement physics of the \
sibling essays. The core essay ",
 Cell["Korotkov-Quantum-Bayesian.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " builds the single-qubit Bayes kick with the coherence riding along, which \
we here promote to two qubits; the essay ",
 Cell["Watching-Two-Axes.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 " watches one qubit along two incompatible axes, where this essay watches \
two qubits along one joint parity axis. The single-qubit purity ride-along, \
the way an ideal measurement leaves the coherence riding on the geometric \
mean of its two populations so a pure state stays pure, is the prerequisite: \
the whole entangling mechanism is that same ride-along, one level up."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell["Notation and Conventions: One Probe, Two Qubits, Three Bins", "Section",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We work in units where the reduced Planck constant is one, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 ". Two qubits, remote and never coupled, are jointly measured by a single \
probe that reflects off both, so its output records the qubit pair. Written \
in the computational basis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"00"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"01"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"10"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"11"},
     "Ket"]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 ", the joint measurement is engineered so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"01"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"10"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 " shift the probe by the same amount: it is a half-parity meter, \
distinguishing three bins, the state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 ", the state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 ", and the odd-parity pair ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"01"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"10"},
     "Ket"]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 ", but never resolving which of the two odd states it holds. The averaged \
record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " over a window is Gaussian about a center ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " that takes three values: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "1"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "4"], "=", "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "3"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " for the odd pair. One rate organizes the measurement, the strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 " set by the measurement efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 "; and one extra rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],
 " carries whatever dephasing survives inside the protected odd subspace \
(imperfect matching of the two centers, photon loss between the cavities). We \
work with the so-called X-state, in which only the two-qubit density-matrix \
elements ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"00", ",", "00"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"11", ",", "11"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"01", ",", "01"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"10", ",", "10"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 ", and the odd-parity coherence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 " are appreciable, because the meter's distinguishability damps every other \
off-diagonal element fast."
}], "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Fix the five surviving X-state numbers as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"]}], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "3"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "4"], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "5"], "}", "=", "{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"00", ",", "00"}]]}], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"01", ",", "01"}]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"10", ",", "10"}]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"11", ",", "11"}]], ",", 
   RowBox[{GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 ". Encode the three-center Gaussian likelihoods for a reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 ", and the concurrence that measures the entanglement of an X-state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"likelis", ",", " ", "concurrence"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"likelis", "[", 
    RowBox[{"v_", ",", " ", "dvv_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "dvv"}], ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
           "dvv"}], "}"}], " ", "-", " ", "v"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"concurrence", "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"2", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "5", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"x", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The concurrence runs from zero for a separable or classically mixed state \
to one for a Bell state, and for this X-state it is set by a race: the \
odd-parity coherence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "5"], "=", GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 " pulling it up against the geometric mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "4"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 " of the two even populations pulling it down."
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the update the essay turns on. Recall from the single-qubit case that a \
Bayesian kick multiplies each population by its Gaussian likelihood and \
renormalizes, while the coherence rides along on the geometric mean of the \
two likelihoods it connects. The two-qubit version is identical, one level \
up: the four populations each pick up their likelihood, and the odd-parity \
coherence rides on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "3"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 ", the geometric mean of the two likelihoods of the states it links, with an \
extra dephasing factor. Encode one honest Bayesian step: draw the reading \
from the mixture the state predicts, then update:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "twoQubitStep", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"twoQubitStep", "[", 
    RowBox[{"dvv_", ",", " ", "ss_", ",", " ", "gt_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], 
    "]"}], "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ss", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "p", ",",
       " ", "nrm"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Clip", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"x", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "dvv"}], ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
           "dvv"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dvar", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"likelis", "[", 
       RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nrm", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
       "p"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"p", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"p", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"p", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"p", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "5", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"p", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"p", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"-", "gt"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "/", "nrm"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell["\<\
That is the entire integrator: draw which bin the record leans toward with \
the current populations as weights, bury it under window noise, and fold the \
reading back into the five numbers, the four populations by classical Bayes \
and the odd coherence by the geometric-mean ride-along.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell["\<\
1. The Odd-Parity Coherence Is the Purity Ride-Along, One Level Up\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The whole entangling mechanism is the single-qubit purity ride-along \
promoted to the odd-parity subspace. In the single-qubit case, because the \
coherence multiplies by the geometric mean of the two population likelihoods, \
the ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "10"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 " is left untouched by every ideal update, so a pure state stays pure. Here \
the same ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"01", ",", "01"}]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"10", ",", "10"}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 " is left untouched, so a coherent superposition inside the odd subspace \
stays coherent while the meter localizes the pair into that subspace. Confirm \
that an ideal update (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 ") leaves that ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"01", ",", "01"}]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"10", ",", "10"}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " unchanged:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"p2", " ", "=", " ", "P2"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"p3", " ", "=", " ", "P3"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"x5", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{"p2", " ", "p3"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"x2", " ", "p2"}], ")"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"x3", " ", "p3"}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x5", "^", "2"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"x2", " ", "x3"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"P2", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"P3", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"x2", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"x3", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ratio is algebraically conserved, so the odd-parity coherence rides its \
two populations exactly as a single qubit's coherence rides its own, which is \
why a measurement that only sorts the pair into the odd bin leaves a fully \
coherent Bell state rather than a classical mixture of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"01"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"10"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 ". Entanglement here is not created by any interaction; it is the coherence \
that was already present surviving the localization, because the meter cannot \
look inside the subspace it is projecting onto."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],

Cell["2. The Half-Parity Meter: Three Bins, One Protected Subspace", "Section",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start the pair in a product of equal superpositions, so all four \
populations are 1/4 and the odd coherence is 1/4 as well. The meter now sorts \
each record into one of three bins. If the record leans toward ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 ", the pair collapses toward the product state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 " and the odd populations drain away; if the record stays near zero, the \
pair is steered into the odd subspace, where the surviving coherence makes it \
the Bell state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"01"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{"10"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 ". Watch one record that lands in the odd bin: track its concurrence, the \
two even populations, and the total odd population:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dvv", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ss", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", "0.15"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "300"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "300"}], "]"}], " ", "0.02"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "4", "]"}], ";", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"twoQubitStep", "[", 
             RowBox[{"dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"gam", " ", "dt"}], ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
             "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",",
               " ", "0.25"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"concurrence", " ", "/@", " ", "traj"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
          "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
          "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], 
          "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.02"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<concurrence\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Rho]00,00\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<\[Rho]11,11\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<odd population\>\""}], 
         "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of measurement time)\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<value\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<one record steered into the entangled subspace\>\""}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "480"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the two even populations drain toward zero while the odd \
population fills toward one, and the concurrence climbs and then eases back: \
the record has projected the pair into the odd subspace and the surviving \
coherence has become genuine entanglement. A different seed would drain the \
odd population instead and collapse to a product state with zero concurrence; \
the outcome is stochastic, set by which bin the noisy record happens to \
favor, with the bin probabilities equal to the initial populations, the Born \
rule again.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell["3. The Sharp Ceiling: A Closed-Form Maximum Concurrence", "Section",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How entangled can a record make the pair, and how does that depend on when \
we look? Because the whole X-state is fixed by the running readout ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 " together with the initial state and the two rates, the concurrence at any \
time is a definite function of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 ", and it is largest for the record that sits exactly at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 ", the most balanced odd-bin outcome. That most-fortunate concurrence is a \
closed form, a race between the extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " that erodes the coherence and the measurement rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " that first builds and then over-localizes it. Encode the maximum \
concurrence and the concurrence-readout relation:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"cmaxCF", ",", " ", "cOfVCF"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gam_", ",", " ", "dvv_", ",", " ", "ss_", ",", " ", "t_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gam"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"dvv", "^", "2"}]}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"dvv", "^", "2"}]}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"cOfVCF", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "gam_", ",", " ", "dvv_", ",", " ", "ss_", ",", " ", "vt_", ",", " ", 
    "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "gam"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"dvv", "^", "2"}]}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cosh", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "vt", " ", "dvv", " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"dvv", "^", "2"}]}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Show that the concurrence-readout relation is largest at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 " and equals the closed-form ceiling there:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"cOfVCF", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "t"}], 
      "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
     RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "t"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"D", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"cOfVCF", "[", 
          RowBox[{
          "gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "vt", ",", " ", 
           "t"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "vt"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"vt", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], 
    "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both are true: the concurrence is stationary in the readout at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 " and the value there is the ceiling, because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["cosh",
   FontSlant->"Plain"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 " is smallest at zero and it sits in the denominator. No record, however \
lucky, can beat the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 " outcome, so the concurrence a continuous measurement can produce has a \
sharp upper limit at every instant, set entirely by the competition of the \
two rates."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell["4. Pulling the Ceiling Out of an Ensemble of Records", "Section",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell["\<\
Now the payoff. The ceiling was derived from the update; the records should \
press against it and never cross it. Run an ensemble from the product start \
and plot every trajectory's concurrence against the closed-form ceiling (this \
cell runs a small ensemble and takes a few seconds):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dvv", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ss", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", "0.15"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "300"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "60"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "300"}], "]"}], " ", "0.02"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"cmat", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
              RowBox[{"900", " ", "+", " ", "k"}], "]"}], ";", "\n", 
             "       ", 
             RowBox[{"concurrence", " ", "/@", " ", 
              RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"twoQubitStep", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"gam", " ", "dt"}], ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", 
                " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                 "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25",
                   ",", " ", "0.25"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}]}], 
            "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
       "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
             " ", "cmat"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.35", "]"}], ",", " ", "Gray"}], 
             "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0.45"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
           "     ", 
           RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             
             RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of measurement time)\>\"", ",", 
              " ", "\"\<concurrence\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{
           "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
            " ", "\"\<records press against the closed-form ceiling\>\""}], ",",
            " ", 
           RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "500"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "t"}], 
            "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"300", " ", "0.02"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", "Thick", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], 
             "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell["\<\
Every trajectory stays below the dashed ceiling, and the luckiest ones ride \
right along it: the closed-form maximum concurrence is exactly the sharp \
cutoff of the simulated distribution, recovered from records without ever \
imposing it. The ceiling rises from zero as the measurement builds coherence \
into concurrence, peaks, and then decays as continued localization and the \
extra dephasing win, so there is an optimal moment to stop measuring.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell["\<\
Look at where the trajectories actually end up, at a fixed late time, across \
a large ensemble:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dvv", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ss", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", "0.15"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "300"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "2000"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"cend", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "k", "]"}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"concurrence", "@", 
            RowBox[{"Last", "@", 
             RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"twoQubitStep", "[", 
                RowBox[{"dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"gam", " ", "dt"}], ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", 
               " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", 
                 ",", " ", "0.25"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
          "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
      RowBox[{"cend", ",", " ", "40", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<final concurrence\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<counts\>\""}], 
         "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<bimodal: a spike at zero and a peak beneath the \
ceiling\>\""}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The distribution is bimodal: a tall spike at zero concurrence from the \
records that collapsed to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 ", and a separate peak of entangled outcomes that pushes up against, but \
never past, the ceiling. The two peaks are the two fates of the pair, a \
product state or the Bell subspace, and the gap between them is why the \
measurement must be conditioned, kept only when the record lands in the odd \
bin."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell["5. What Sets the Ceiling, and Where This Update Lives", "Section",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The height of the ceiling is a trade-off between the extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 " and the measurement rate. A slow, clean measurement builds coherence into \
concurrence before losing it; a noisy or lossy one erodes the coherence \
faster than it can localize the pair, and the peak concurrence drops. Read \
the peak of the ceiling for three values of the extra dephasing, keyed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dvv", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ss", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "800"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0.05", ",", " ", "0.15", ",", " ", "0.4"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "#"}], 
           "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nst", "]"}], " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.05", ",", " ", "0.15", ",", " ", "0.4"}], "}"}]}], 
        "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell["\<\
As expected, the peak concurrence falls as the extra dephasing grows: a \
nearly ideal channel reaches deep into the entangled regime, while a lossy \
one barely leaves the separable one. This is exactly the trade-off that \
limited the first remote-qubit experiments, where two transmons a meter \
apart, joined only by a coaxial cable and a shared probe, reached a peak \
concurrence around a third before intrinsic dephasing and the finite \
efficiency of the amplifier stopped the climb.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The update we ran is the same one those experiments are analyzed with. Two \
qubits in separate cavities, probed in sequence so the signal reflects off \
one and then the other, are a cascaded system whose joint measurement is \
exactly this half-parity meter; the diagonal elements follow classical Bayes \
and the odd-parity coherence rides the geometric mean, which is the whole \
content of ",
 Cell[BoxData["twoQubitStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 ". The most-likely-path analysis of the ensemble splits into three branches, \
the high-concurrence odd branch that hugs the ceiling and the two \
low-concurrence branches that collapse to the product states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 ", matching the bimodal histogram. And the essay beside this one, ",
 Cell["Watching-Two-Axes.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 ", is the same physics seen the other way: there one qubit is watched along \
two incompatible axes and diffuses on a great circle; here two qubits are \
watched along one parity axis and are steered into a Bell state. In both, the \
state is moved not by any Hamiltonian but by the information a noisy record \
carries, folded back by Bayes' rule."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us (and What Comes Next)", "Section",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell["\<\
You now have a complete, computation-first toolkit for two qubits entangled \
by a joint half-parity measurement: a three-center likelihood, a Bayesian \
step that updates four populations classically and rides the odd-parity \
coherence on their geometric mean, a demonstration that this ride-along is \
the single-qubit purity ride-along one level up, a single record steered into \
a Bell state, a closed-form ceiling on the concurrence recovered from an \
ensemble of records, and the trade-off between measurement rate and dephasing \
that sets its height. Before moving on, the points that were computed and \
verified along the way:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell["\<\
The two-qubit Bayesian update is the single-qubit one on a larger state: four \
populations update by classical Bayes, and the odd-parity coherence rides on \
the geometric mean of its two likelihoods.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The odd-parity ride-along conserves ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"01", ",", "01"}]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"10", ",", "10"}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 " exactly, so a measurement that only sorts the pair into the odd bin leaves \
a coherent Bell state, not a classical mixture; entanglement is the coherence \
surviving localization."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A half-parity meter sorts each record into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 ", or the odd subspace, with bin probabilities equal to the initial \
populations; a record that lands in the odd bin is stochastically steered \
into a Bell state."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The concurrence at any instant is a definite function of the readout, \
largest at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 ", so it has a sharp closed-form ceiling that rises from zero, peaks, and \
decays."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell["\<\
An ensemble of records presses against that ceiling and never crosses it, and \
the final-concurrence distribution is bimodal: a spike at zero from the \
collapsed records and a peak beneath the ceiling from the entangled ones.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell["\<\
The ceiling's height is a trade-off between the extra dephasing and the \
measurement rate, the same trade-off that capped the first remote-qubit \
experiments near a third.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell["\<\
The natural continuations are the pieces this essay set aside: the full \
four-by-four state with the fast-damping off-diagonal elements restored, the \
cavity and probe fields the half-parity meter is built from, real-time \
feedback that stabilizes the entanglement instead of only heralding it, and \
the many-qubit parity measurements that turn this single joint check into the \
continuously monitored error syndrome of a stabilizer code, which is where \
the non-commuting essay's Bacon-Shor connection and this essay's parity meter \
meet.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
